@startuml
title Iterator / Cursor

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Provide sequential access to elements without exposing representation.

**Motivation**:
Collections expose uniform iteration semantics (for-each).

**Applicability**:
Provide multiple traversal strategies; decouple structure from traversal.

**Participants**:
Aggregate creates iterator; Iterator navigates.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Uniform traversal; multiple iterators concurrently.
Cons: Fail-fast vs. snapshot semantics; concurrent modification issues.

**Implementation Notes**:
Provide external vs internal iteration; generator/yield in languages supporting it.

**Known Uses**:
Java Iterator, Iterable; Python iterators/generators.

**Related Patterns**:
Composite (tree traversal), Visitor (processing while iterating).

endlegend

interface Iterator {
  +hasNext() : boolean
  +next() : Element
}

interface Aggregate {
  +createIterator() : Iterator
}

class ConcreteIterator
class ConcreteAggregate

Iterator <|.. ConcreteIterator
Aggregate <|.. ConcreteAggregate
ConcreteAggregate o-- ConcreteIterator : creates
@enduml